    "narrative": "The crown jewel of tonight\u2019s lineup is undoubtedly **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts a massive 87.14 efficiency score. Facing Sugano, who carries a shaky 5.02 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime position to leverage his elite sprint speed against a high-contact pitcher; the combination of the favorable matchup and his high-leverage spot in the two-hole makes him our primary anchor for both SB and R potential. **Gabriel Moreno** follows closely with a 71.10, benefiting from the same exploitable matchup against Sugano. We are also projecting significant upside from **Brice Turang** (67.46) and **Seiya Suzuki** (64.98). **Seiya Suzuki** is a particularly intriguing play; while he typically faces platoon headwinds, the scouting report on the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery (87% SB success rate) significantly bumps his value as a dual-threat option tonight.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Travis Bazzana** on the bench. With a score of 39.30, he narrowly missed our \"Marginal\" threshold of 40.0. While he offers a decent park factor (+5%), he is neutralized by Anderson\u2019s sharp xERA (3.28) and the overall difficulty of the matchup, which forced us to prioritize the higher-floor upside of **Henry Bolte** and **Mickey Moniak**. We must also monitor the situation in the middle infield carefully: **Cole Young** is currently sitting at a marginal 42.79, but he carries a 31% rain risk that could lead to a shortened game or an outright postponement, making him the most volatile asset in our lineup. Finally, while we are thin on power depth tonight with **James Wood**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** sidelined, we are banking on the speed-heavy profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** to carry the load against these exploitable arms.",
